### ============================================================
### Kind Mental Health App — API Test Script
###
### HOW TO USE (IntelliJ / HTTP Client):
###   1. Open this file in IntelliJ IDEA.
###   2. Select the "dev" environment (top-right dropdown).
###   3. Run requests 1-to-114 in order, top-to-bottom.
###      The login handler auto-fills {{token}} and all
###      create handlers auto-fill their {{...Id}} variables.
###
### RE-RUNNING: If register returns 409, the test email
###   already exists. Either change the email in requests
###   [1] and [2] to something new, or run request [0] first
###   to delete the leftover record.
### ============================================================

### [0] PRE-CLEAN — delete leftover test user from a previous
###     run (ignore 404 if this is your first run)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/email/kindtest@kind.com
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ── AUTH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [1] Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kind Test User",
  "email": "kindtest@kind.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

###

### [2] Login — captures JWT token for all subsequent requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kindtest@kind.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
  client.global.set("userEmail", response.body.email);
%}

###

### ── USERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [3] Get all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### [4] Get user by email — captures userId for later steps
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/email/kindtest@kind.com
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {%
  client.global.set("userId", response.body.id);
%}

###

### [5] Get user by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### [6] Create a secondary user (conflict test)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Second User",
  "email": "second@kind.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

###

### [7] Update notification settings (enable)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/notifications?enabled=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### [8] Complete intro for user
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/complete-intro
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### [9] Update user details
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Kind Test User Updated",
  "email": "kindtest@kind.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

###

### ── EMOTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [10] Create emotion (HAPPY)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/emotions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Joyful",
  "moodCategory": "HAPPY"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("emotionId", response.body.id);
%}

###

### [11] Create emotion (SAD)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/emotions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

